
 CHANGES.DOC                                                      09/09/1993
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  VER # DATE       DESCRIPTION
  ===== ========== ========================================================
  1.27* 09/09/1993  o  Changes documentation is now upside down as you can
                       see. :-)

                    o  You can now change the blue color in chat to any of
                       the following ones. Adjust COLOR slider in PCONFIG.

                       0 = Black     4 = Blue
                       1 = Red       5 = Purple
                       2 = Green     6 = Cyan
                       3 = Yellow    7 = White

                    o  Clearing chat didn't reset line counter, fixed.

                    o  You can run PCONFIG and OVER also from Workbench.

                    o  Several minor fixes and optimizations.
  ----- ---------- --------------------------------------------------------
  1.26  30/07/1993  o  Chat macros can now use following control codes.

                       \n = Linefeed
                       \b = Beep and flash
                       \w = One second delay
                       \\ = Single slash

                    o  Pager now supports multiple languages. Set LANGUAGE
                       in PCONFIG and create text files for all languages.
                       Move these files to your BBS text directories, each
                       language should have own directory there. Make sure
                       you have only file names (no dir names) in the path
                       config. You can also leave LANGUAGE unset and texts
                       will work as before.

                    o  Overrider supports KS3 newlook pull-down menus.
  ----- ---------- --------------------------------------------------------
  1.25  12/07/1993  o  PCONFIG will now work properly on 2 color screens.

                    o  AUTO checkbox added to OVER and pager windows. It's
                       used to select if AUTO macro is sent in the chat.
  ----- ---------- --------------------------------------------------------
  1.24  20/06/1993  o  E!-PAGER has been tested to work on Amiga 1200.

                    o  Chat will run even if userinfo is not available.

                    o  Sysop name wasn't always displayed in chat, fixed.

                    o  Problems with checkboxes in PCONFIG, fixed.

                    o  RANDOM meter was forgotten from 1.2 release, fixed.

                    o  STEPBYSTEP meter didn't work correctly, fixed.
  ----- ---------- --------------------------------------------------------
  1.23* 07/06/1993  o  You can select LAYOUT and OVERWRITE modes automati-
                       cally by checking corresponding options in PCONFIG.

                    o  There are two new gadgets in PCONFIG macro window.

                        TAB: String sent when the tabulator is selected.

                       AUTO: This is automatically sent when chat begins.

                    o  There are also two new commands in the chat.

                       CTRL-B: Saves current chat buffer to disk.

                       CTRL-U: Loads a file to current chat buffer.

                    o  Cursor sometimes disappeared in the chat, fixed.

                    o  All executables can be made resident.
  ----- ---------- --------------------------------------------------------
  1.22* 06/06/1993  o  No length limit in page window SYSOP LABEL, fixed.

                    o  You can use arrow keys to scroll the chat buffer.

                       PCONFIG can be used to select the size of this text
                       buffer. Enter number of lines allowed for each chat
                       window to the BUFFER gadget. Box next to this shows
                       how much memory would the chat try to allocate.

                       Currently this buffer doesn't grow or automatically
                       destroy stuff to get memory for new text. It simply
                       blinks the screen when the buffer is full. User can
                       press CTRL-L or move up to continue.

                    o  Chat will ignore forbidden characters, no spaces.

                    o  Sysop can use CTRL-S to switch windows in the chat.

                    o  CTRL-O can be used in chat to select between insert
                       and overwrite modes. Insert currently inserts chars
                       only in the current line.

                    o  CTRL-A in screen chat will toggle the layout mode.

                    o  Chat now supports function key macros. Select FKEYS
                       in PCONFIG and a window with string gadgets appears
                       so you can define one macro string for each key. If
                       you press one of the ten function keys in the split
                       screen chat, this previously defined text is sent.

                    o  Tabulator corresponds eight (8) spaces in the chat.

                    o  PLOGS can also be executed from the CLI.

                    o  Fixed several minor bugs.
  ----- ---------- --------------------------------------------------------
  1.21  30/05/1993  o  Chat didn't check terminal lines properly, fixed.

                    o  You can use arrow keys in split screen chat to move
                       left and right in the current line.

                    o  Chat will reset IPL codes after the quit command.

                    o  SysOp Available option in Master System Options can
                       be used by selecting 'MASTER' in the Overrider.

                    o  SYSOP LABEL can also be changed in the page window.
  ----- ---------- --------------------------------------------------------
  1.20  29/05/1993  o  Third major release.
  ===== ========== ========================================================

  If there is an asterisk (*) after the version number, you must run config
  before using the update, select CONTINUE if and when a requester appears.

 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 09/09/1993                                                      CHANGES.DOC

